{"custom_id":"s-ap_statistics-m05-k1","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfyk5VMGeKrBBZLNRQfmj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"**Answer: B (index 1).** Removing the circled point makes the correlation stronger and the least-squares line noticeably steeper.\n\n1. **The other 11 points:** They run from (6.3, 49.5) to (15.2, 75.5) in a tight, positive, nearly straight pattern. The slope from first to last is about (75.5 − 49.5) / (15.2 − 6.3) ≈ 26 / 8.9 ≈ 2.9 mpg per liter.\n2. **The circled point:** At (29.9, 76.6) it sits far to the right of the other x-values, so it has high leverage. If the trend of the other points continued, an x of 29.9 would predict roughly 75.5 + 2.9 × 14.7 ≈ 118 mpg. Its actual value, 76.6, is far below that.\n3. **Effect on the line:** Because the point is so far right and so far below the trend, it pulls the right end of the fitted line down. That makes the slope much flatter. Removing it lets the line steepen back to about 2.9.\n4. **Effect on the correlation:** The point also breaks up the linear pattern. Without it, the remaining points fit a line closely, so the correlation gets stronger.\n\nThis rules out A (slope about the same), C (less steep) and D (weaker correlation). The item is clear as written."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QtNc8hZogj7CRQCiDC1xVt","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"1","choice_index":1,"final_answer":"Correlation stronger, slope noticeably steeper","brief_reasoning":"The other 11 points are strongly linear with a slope of about 2.9. The removed point has high leverage and lies far below that trend, so it flattens the line and weakens r. Removing it makes the line steeper and the correlation stronger.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":571,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":773,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":150},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":571,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":773,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":150},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"cost":0.0179712}
{"custom_id":"s-ap_statistics-m08-k0","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfyk5iQbAuP1N5ynM1Yw3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The normal model works here, and the probability comes out to about 0.958.\n\n**Checking the conditions**\n- Large counts: np = 200 × 0.6 = 120 and n(1 − p) = 200 × 0.4 = 80. Both are at least 10.\n- 10% condition: the sample of 200 is far less than 10% of the 40,000 voters.\n\n**Mean and standard deviation of p̂**\n- The mean is 0.6.\n- The standard deviation is √(0.6 × 0.4 / 200) = √0.0012 ≈ 0.034641.\n\n**Probability**\n- z = (0.66 − 0.6) / 0.034641 ≈ 1.732\n- P(Z < 1.732) ≈ 0.9584, which rounds to 0.958.\n\nThe other choices are wrong for these reasons:\n- 0.042 is the upper tail, P(p̂ > 0.66), not the lower tail the question asks for.\n- 0.549 doesn't match either tail.\n- The normal model doesn't require p = 0.5, so the \"not appropriate\" choice is wrong."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0198Koi4og9Pu4y8EHP5RkMZ","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"1","choice_index":3,"final_answer":"Conditions met; P ≈ 0.958","brief_reasoning":"np=120 and n(1-p)=80 are both at least 10, and the sample is under 10% of the population. SD=√(0.24/200)≈0.03464, z≈1.732, so P≈0.958.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":381,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":535,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":381,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":535,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_token